ures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan inventory corrected for an existing anti-migration guard: tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py::test_flush_cas_loop_stays_in_yaml_verbatim_shape must be rewritten in the cutover change, not merely allowed to fail. It will pin the new single push-only strict canary step, synchronous override, absence of inline CAS/raw git, preserved red disposition, and updated file-level rationale.","timestamp":1786147905202013001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: expanded both workflow invocations to the complete argparse-valid shapes (`--tracker .`, reconciler `--message`, `--author-name`, and `--author-email`), split the escaped acceptance-criteria lines, explicitly covered the stale sibling rationale in `test_no_logic_bearing_rebar_calls_left_in_yaml`, and added the two merge-command-dependent workflow tests discovered by exact-command grep. File impact now includes both newly identified test files. The interrupted review had validated these as the grounded defects; rerunning from the corrected material.","timestamp":1786164930261090001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD contract card and parity census for 742d:\n\n- authoritative_contract: ticket ACs plus current workflow red-on-persistent-failure behavior and the landed private CLI in src/rebar/_store/push.py.\n- trigger_preconditions: reconciler exact run block starts with a dirty real tracker under project sync.push=off; canary exact run block starts clean but one commit ahead; strict-failure cases use a real bare origin with a rejecting pre-receive hook.\n- production_path: parse each named GitHub Actions step, substitute only the run-id expression, and execute the exact shell with the worktree venv against real temporary git repositories.\n- test_tier: executable workflow subprocess + real git refs; a source-only assertion is one tier too low because it cannot prove argparse, env, commit identity, delivery, exit code, or pending-commit behavior.\n- observable_postcondition: reconciler exits 0, pushes the dirty event, and the remote commit has the exact subject and supplied author despite sync.push=off; rejection exits nonzero and keeps the local commit. Canary pushes an ahead commit; policy rejection exits nonzero and keeps it pending.\n- collateral_invariants: unrelated files and remote history remain intact; no empty commit; working tree clean after successful reconciler commit; rejected local commit remains reachable.\n- negative_control: project sync.push=off without the workflow's REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always would not deliver; the exact block must override it.\n- recovery/contention: no new retry implementation is introduced; both calls ride the already-locked core seam, so existing in-process push suites own rejection→fetch→merge→re-push contention. No new contention harness is warranted.\n- ci_gate: exact nodes collected/executed under make test; focused run first, then make lint/typecheck/test.\n\nSurface parity: CLI/private process boundary = in scope through both exact workflow blocks; automated callers = in scope, one executable test per workflow; library facade = out of scope/no contract change, existing best-effort tests retained; MCP/API = out of scope/no call-path change; dual-direction/inbound Jira application = out of scope because this cutover changes only outbound tickets delivery.","timestamp":1786166249784384001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1538 (e462f811, Change-Id Ia8b5fcb6fc89703390b2b1eb57d324f00436d59e). Before push: fetched origin, rebased onto origin/main (no-op), proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then reran 47 affected tests, lint/actionlint, typecheck, and diff check green. Held-out real-git workflow oracle passed 2/2 and rejected strict/authorship mutations. Waiting for independent LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit.","timestamp":1786167236384641001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed as Gerrit change 1538, commit 11a026540b on origin/main. Gate evidence: LLM-Review +1; Verified +1 from GitHub run 31241954882; zero unresolved comments. TDD evidence: six contract nodes RED before implementation; implementer saw four happy-path nodes only; two executable real-git workflow tests were physically held out and passed 2/2 on first restore; mutations removing canary --strict and reconciler --author-email each made the held-out oracle RED; affected suite passed 47 tests plus lint/actionlint and typecheck. Full CI passed across all matrices and integration tiers.","timestamp":1786168472776133001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion-verifier remediation evidence: the reconciler standing-decision block at .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml lines 25-31 now states that the final strict core adapter commits when needed and synchronously pushes dirty or clean-ahead state, keeping the workflow red on failure. The canary standing-decision block at .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml lines 14-19 already states that the strict synchronous adapter delegates CAS recovery to rebar._store.push. scripts/canary_bridge.py lines 1-5 and tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py lines 1-12, 63-98 document and enforce the same reversal. External gate evidence for the [operator-attested] test criterion remains CI run 31241954882: focused workflow coverage, lint/actionlint, typecheck, default suites, and integration suites all passed across the full matrix.","timestamp":1786168998761520001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verifier-driven follow-up pushed as Gerrit change 1540 (commit e8a3874, Change-Id retained by hook). It corrects the reconciler standing-decision block that still claimed the engine never pushes. Before push: fetched origin, rebased onto origin/main, proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then reran the 16 focused workflow tests, lint/actionlint, and diff check green. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; ticket remains in progress.","timestamp":1786169095483486001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Verifier follow-up landed as Gerrit change 1540, commit 039fe7bbde on origin/main. Gate evidence: LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 from CI run 31243115851, and zero unresolved comments. The reconciler and canary standing-decision blocks now both describe strict synchronous core-owned delivery; focused 16-test workflow oracle and lint/actionlint passed locally after the mandatory origin/main refresh.","timestamp":1786170300725928001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Execution-phase review found the final stale synthetic raw-git exemption rationale. Remediated the ticket into a post-land closeout plan and pushed the one-line cleanup as Gerrit change 1541 (e04c0e69ab). Before push: fetched/rebased origin/main, proved 0 behind / 1 ahead, then 46 focused tests, lint/actionlint, and commit-hook mypy passed. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; no force close.","timestamp":1786171482070659001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 1541 CI rerun 31266912051 remained non-real: py3.11 repeated known flake fade-ea90-7564-4715 (gw3 crash in test_matching_guard_is_accepted after 11,435 passes); py3.12 exposed a separate temp-fixture git merge conflict after 11,434 passes, filed as cb9c-49cb-5aba-488d and linked discovered_from. The one-line raw-git fixture-comment change cannot affect either test. Other matrices/gates passed; posting another recheck, never bypassing Verified.","timestamp":1786207480573223001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final closeout evidence: Gerrit 1541 merged as origin/main 511c339a63878f2c331a8cf4da56b8d5cc74e6d5. It passed LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 in CI run 31269583553, and has zero unresolved comments. The merged change replaces the stale synthetic raw-git fixture rationale, satisfying the final unchecked acceptance criterion without changing runtime behavior or the continuity contracts retained by changes 1538 and 1540.","timestamp":1786211548961456001}],"created_at":1786142486742185001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ad97ac7e-3273-4695-866d-b100d9633851","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a"},{"link_uuid":"3b895837-aaa7-4161-921c-0d6de841cfaf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"266d-dd93-01b6-4d5f"},{"link_uuid":"be16e163-2430-4c72-a4b4-01bc6945db9a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6318-7e48-c879-478a"},{"link_uuid":"bdee25fa-5f0e-446c-b166-0ba7ca3bc017","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a576-a4db-ae47-4a10"},{"link_uuid":"64c038d3-93e8-4cc3-9237-e84e3324a574","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4dc0-731b-be37-40f8"}],"description":"## Completion state\n\nThis workflow migration is complete. Gerrit changes 1538, 1540, and 1541 are merged. The current tree is the intended post-migration state:\n\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml delegates one strict synchronous commit-and-push action to the core bridge runner while preserving the exact bot identity and commit subject.\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml delegates one strict synchronous push-only action to rebar._store.push.\n- Both workflow-local CAS loops and the reconciler raw-git exemption are absent.\n- Core owns retry/CAS recovery and workflow calls remain red on exhausted delivery.\n- Python library and MCP defaults remain best-effort; this ticket changes only the strict workflow adapters.\n- Older workflows and environments continue through the retained legacy reconcile and push contracts.\n- The stale synthetic test rationale was replaced by the generic reviewed-fixture wording in Gerrit 1541; there is no remaining implementation task.\n\n## Verification\n\nRepository checks at merged ref 694cf894def36241724e7049e3308d782037ef6d:\n- execute the focused workflow and raw-git lint suites plus make lint;\n- confirm both workflow run blocks contain one core push entrypoint and no inline fetch/merge/retry loop;\n- confirm tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py contains the generic reviewed-workflow rationale;\n- confirm rtk proxy rg -n \"4c4f|keeps the CAS loop in YAML\" tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py returns no match;\n- execute the real-git workflow smoke tests for successful delivery and rejected-push red failure.\n\nThe change rides existing locked core operations and introduces no new retry/cache/composed write, so existing push contention suites remain the correct concurrency oracle.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThe migration centralizes delivery mechanics without narrowing any public surface. CLI workflow adapters use strict delivery; Python and MCP retain best-effort defaults. Exact reconciler identity/subject and older vocabulary remain available. Reverting the workflow call sites restores the prior inline loops and requires no data migration; pending local commits remain recoverable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both inline workflow CAS loops are absent.\n- [x] Each workflow invokes exactly one complete core push action.\n- [x] Strict workflow delivery remains synchronous and red on exhausted failure.\n- [x] Python library and MCP push defaults remain best-effort.\n- [x] Reconciler author identity and exact commit subject are preserved.\n- [x] The reconciler raw-git exemption is removed.\n- [x] Standing decisions and executable tests state that core owns retry/CAS recovery.\n- [x] Real-git workflow smoke tests preserve successful delivery and rejected-push failure.\n- [x] Copied-template migration, timing, and rollback continuity are documented.\n- [x] tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py contains no stale ticket-4c4f CAS-loop rationale.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Gerrit changes 1538, 1540, and 1541 passed LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments before merge.\n  provenance: environment=Gerrit and GitHub Actions runs 31241954882, 31243115851, and 31269583553; principal=project review and CI bots; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the actual project review and CI systems evaluated the merged workflow changes.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"replace dirty commit-back CAS loop with strict core entrypoint and preserve bot identity"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml","reason":"replace client-template flush loop with synchronous strict core call while preserving red disposition"},{"path":"scripts/canary_bridge.py","reason":"update obsolete standing decision that prohibited core ownership"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py","reason":"replace YAML-loop extraction with executable workflow-block continuity tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py","reason":"update anti-migration assertions and both stale rationales for core-owned push"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py","reason":"retire YAML-local merge assertion removed with both inline CAS loops"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py","reason":"preserve merge-driver ordering contract without requiring a canary YAML-local merge"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"document copied canary-template shape and refresh action"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"document opt-in migration and no-cleanup rollback for existing copied workflows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1786437617673074001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a"],["parent","1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770"],["relates_to","266d-dd93-01b6-4d5f"],["relates_to","4dc0-731b-be37-40f8"],["relates_to","6318-7e48-c879-478a"],["relates_to","a576-a4db-ae47-4a10"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770","parent_status_uuid":"f0ef9d02-663b-465f-a82e-e574ab30ebb4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bridge","ci","workflow"],"ticket_id":"742d-54f1-3b6f-4864","ticket_type":"task","title":"Migrate both bridge workflows to core push entrypoints","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["dc2c534d-cf3a-4b5a-a41f-beead5a43c2e","21e4a7a4-7928-4aa2-a1a3-89fd8a9e831b","6face1ea-126f-470c-b69d-b08f3ad4d68a","667d27df-30ed-49d0-8e7e-bbccfe24b467","f35a2b03-4828-4a2e-bb9d-14593b4c4948","4ce25b84-e618-49f7-a647-b4527ee67f12","3cb7f700-8aca-4185-8784-e97f8841781a","25f3e742-e6c4-4285-bb78-2776cc97bc82","2900a3f3-2b2c-4611-9bb2-c2fe6f829857","88fb0d29-efea-4f0a-a124-32cf46f0f231","0f7f41e8-ac45-4de7-8469-049a022295a8","aab2b42f-50c7-44f7-bb53-295f9a96061e","7c6a33e5-e7e2-4c68-adc9-168540c71a55","f0ef9d02-663b-465f-a82e-e574ab30ebb4","e56716a5-338d-4793-8f81-ce77629adf85"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659620652041001,"uuid":"55e552ad-5e96-4a5d-91eb-92394ff7701e"}